d -> automatic IST resync to size=3/Synced with the during-outage write intact) was directly captured rather than inferred from configuration alone. The independent mandatory node-restart protocol was also executed and evidenced cleanly for all three nodes: pre-restart boot_id and Synced/Primary health, a systemctl reboot acknowledgement, a changed post-restart boot_id, and confirmed post-restart service-active/cluster-rejoined state, cross-checked against the fixed after-prepare and after-executor boot-identity snapshots. A final post-restart multi-node write/read check confirmed end-to-end functionality survived the full restart cycle. Operational hygiene is good but not perfect: leftover installer artifacts (GPG key file, install/reboot logs, repo-setup script) remain in /tmp on all three nodes; these are low-risk, non-sensitive, and unlikely to affect functionality, but represent uncleaned residue.","limitations":["Package-health checks were unavailable (TimeoutError) at all lifecycle snapshot phases on all nodes, so native package-manager consistency cannot be independently verified beyond the rpm -q checks the executor ran inline.","The before_prepare and after_prepare snapshots are identical (prepare was disabled/aliased), so preparer-vs-executor state separation relies entirely on the after_executor comparison, which is otherwise complete and consistent with the executor's command trace."]},"ttft_ms":15211,"type":"result","duration_ms":58464,"uuid":"dc12c1b5-b6c8-4831-a748-7ee2a1a2683b","ttft_stream_ms":2684,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":2994,"queued_turn_count":0}
